 -Darchunit.freeze.store.default.allowStoreCreation=true
 ----
 
+To repair the integrity of an existing store on initialization, configure
+`freeze.store.default.integrity=repair` (the default is `ignore`, which performs no integrity checks).
+Every initialization checks the current index and files on disk, even if the store was already initialized.
+Repair removes entries whose paths are invalid or do not point to regular files directly within the store folder.
+It also removes entries and their files when no violations remain, including files containing only line breaks.
+For symbolic links to resolved files, both the link and its target are deleted.
+Entries sharing a file name or referring to the same file, including through symbolic or hard links, are left untouched,
+as are files not referenced by any entry.
+In repair mode, saving an empty list of violations forgets a known rule instead of storing an empty file.
+Its file is deleted unless another entry refers to it; an unknown rule with no violations is not stored.
+If the file cannot be deleted, saving fails and the rule's entry is retained.
+
 It is also possible to allow all violations to be "refrozen", i.e. the store will just be updated
 with the current state, and the reported result will be success. Thus, it is effectively the same behavior
 as if all rules would never have been frozen.
